# {{.Name}}

A Sora network-hook extension (DPI-bypass fragments).

> **Status: contract per `reports/extensions-40/spec-net-hooks.md`.** The
> manifest side is real; core-side compilation of fragments is not
> implemented yet.

## hook.json (L1: declarative engine fragments)

No extension code runs on the traffic path - the engine compiles these
fragments into its own config:

- `hook_version: 1`
- `engine_fragments[]`: `engines` (e.g. `sing-box`), `match`
  (`domain_suffix` here), `params` - strictly per-engine (allowlisted,
  typed, ranged). An unknown param rejects the whole fragment.
- Fragments merge into the session plan as a named extension layer; on
  conflict with user settings **the user wins**.

No MITM by design: a hook gets no keys, installs no CA, decrypts nothing.

## Ship

```sh
sora-ext validate
sora-ext pack . -o {{.ID}}.soraext
sora-ext sign --key .sora/author.key {{.ID}}.soraext
```

The `net.hooks` permission is **dangerous**: the install prompt requires
explicit confirmation, and updates that add it re-prompt the user.
